---
// Terms of use. The app license itself rests on Apple's standard EULA; this page
// supplements it with what's specific to Gather Scanner (prices, corrections,
// disclaimers) and covers the website. Plain-English and first person to match the
// rest of the site. Keep in sync with the privacy policy.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { site, links, withBase } from "../data/site";

const effectiveDate = "July 5, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={`Terms of Use — ${site.name}`} description={`The terms for using ${site.name} and this website.`}>
  <main class="flex-grow w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-page-margin py-16 flex flex-col gap-10">
    <a
      class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors font-label-md self-start"
      href={withBase("/")}>← Back to Gather Scanner</a
    >

    <header class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h1 class="text-display font-display text-on-surface">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="text-label-sm font-label-sm text-text-muted">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="bg-surface-elevated p-6 rounded-2xl border border-surface-border flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">The short version</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Use the app for what it's for: tracking your collection. Card prices are estimates, not
        appraisals. If you choose to share scan corrections, you're letting me use them to train
        the scanner. The app is provided as-is by one person doing his best. These terms cover
        both the Gather Scanner app and this website.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">The app license</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Your license to use Gather Scanner is
        <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" rel="noopener">Apple's standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a>,
        which applies to apps distributed through the App Store. The terms on this page
        supplement that agreement with the parts specific to Gather Scanner. If they conflict,
        Apple's agreement wins for anything about the license itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Purchases</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        The Unlimited unlock is a one-time in-app purchase processed by Apple. Payment, billing,
        and refunds are handled entirely through Apple and follow
        <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/" rel="noopener">Apple's media services terms</a>.
        I never see your payment details and can't issue refunds directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Card prices are estimates</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Price data comes from third-party sources and is provided for your information only. I
        don't guarantee that prices are accurate, current, or complete, and they aren't
        appraisals or financial advice. Before buying, selling, or trading cards for real money,
        verify prices with the marketplace you're actually using.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Shared scan corrections</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Sharing corrections is optional and off by default; what a correction contains is
        described in the
        <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href={withBase("/privacy#whats-shared")}>privacy policy</a>.
        If you opt in, you grant me a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free license to use your
        shared corrections to train and improve Gather Scanner's card-recognition models. Models
        trained this way may also power related products I build in the future. Because
        submissions are anonymous, they can't be identified or withdrawn after they're sent;
        opting out stops future sharing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Fair use of the app and site</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-2 text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        <li>Don't use the app or website in ways that break the law or infringe others' rights.</li>
        <li>Don't submit deliberately false, abusive, or junk content through correction sharing.</li>
        <li>Don't attempt to disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorized access to the services behind the app or this site.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Magic: The Gathering</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Gather Scanner is unofficial Fan Content permitted under the
        <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href="https://company.wizards.com/en/legal/fancontentpolicy" rel="noopener">Wizards of the Coast Fan Content Policy</a>.
        It is not approved or endorsed by Wizards of the Coast and is not affiliated with
        Wizards of the Coast or Hasbro, Inc. Portions of the materials used, including card
        names and card images, are property of Wizards of the Coast LLC. ©Wizards of the Coast
        LLC. Magic: The Gathering® is a trademark of Wizards of the Coast LLC. For more
        information about Wizards of the Coast and its trademarks, visit
        <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href="https://company.wizards.com/" rel="noopener">company.wizards.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">No warranty, limited liability</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Gather Scanner and this website are provided "as is" and "as available," without
        warranties of any kind, express or implied, to the maximum extent permitted by law. To
        the same extent, I am not liable for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential
        damages arising from your use of the app or site, and my total liability for any claim
        is limited to the amount you paid for the app. Nothing here limits rights you have under
        law that can't be limited by agreement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        If these terms change, this page will be updated and the effective date above will
        change. Continuing to use the app or site after a change means you accept the updated
        terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Governing law</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York, United States, without
        regard to its conflict-of-law rules.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-headline-md text-on-surface">Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md font-body-md text-on-surface-variant">
        Email <a class="text-primary hover:text-primary-fixed transition-colors" href={links.support}>support@gatherscanner.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
